                "content": "The ALL operator is used to compare a value \nto every value returned by a subquery.\n\nThe ALL operator evaluates to TRUE if \nevery value in the subquery result-set meet the condition.\n\nThe ALL operator is typically used with\nWHERE and HAVING statements.\n\nALL Syntax\n\n SELECT column_name(s)\n\n FROM table_name\n\n WHERE \n column_name operator ALL (subquery);\n\nNote: The operator must be a standard comparison \noperator (=, <>, !=, >, >=, <, or <=).",
                "heading": "The SQL ALL Operator"
